values ('Victoria National Golf Club', 'Lamar, IN', null, 1998, 'Victoria National Golf Course is a private 18-hole golf course located northeast of Newburgh, Indiana, in the southwestern corner of the state, roughly seven miles east of Evansville. Victoria was designed by golf course architect Tom Fazio and constructed in 1996 on land that had been used for strip mines from the 1950s until 1977. Developed and initially owned by Terry Friedman and family, the course was sold to Victoria Partners LLC in 2010. In 2018 it was purchased by the Dormie Network.', 'http://www.victorianational.com/', 'opengolfapi', 'dfd21ea9-4cdb-47c5-9b78-4a15f8dd2480', now())
